From: mpc-pi
Subject: [PATCH] nec: exact V33 idle-iteration recorder and skip

The MPC2000XL OS spends most of its guest time in a RAM-resident main
scheduler loop (linear 0x0077f under OS v1.20), a second recorded head covers the tick-counter wait loop at linear 0x01691,
and a third head plus a one-port I/O read whitelist admits the DMA-ready poll
at 0x36115. The whitelist records a side-effect-free status-port read into
the verified set; the recorder correctly never arms that loop, because the
V53's internal DMA advances synchronously with CPU execution, so the port is
not slice-stable - the self-validation is the point: eleven service calls that
poll task flags and queues, then jump back. A guest-PC histogram put the loop
and its callees at the top of a profile in which twenty 64-byte regions cover
72.5% of all executed instructions.

MAME_MPC_V53_IDLE_SKIP records one full loop iteration: its live-in reads
(reads not preceded by the iteration's own write to the same address), the
value each written address held before the iteration's first write, and its
cycle cost. The iteration closes as skippable only if the registers, segment
registers, flags, prefetch count, mode bits and repeat state form a fixed
point, every written address holds its pre-iteration value again at the loop
head (the same stack slot re-pushed by each call satisfies this by
first-write dedup), no I/O access occurred and no external interrupt was
dispatched. While armed, and only when no interrupt is pending, whole
iterations are charged against m_icount without executing; the remainder
smaller than one iteration always executes normally, so a timeslice boundary
or interrupt lands mid-loop exactly as it would have unskipped. Within one
timeslice no other device runs, which is what makes the once-per-timeslice
read-set verification exact; any change re-records from scratch.

Software interrupts (BRK) inside the iteration are normal control flow and
are recorded through the same hooked accessors, including the BRK88/BRKFD
HLE paths. External interrupts abort a recording in progress.

An env-gated per-instruction guest-PC histogram (MAME_MPC_V53_PC_HISTOGRAM)
is included as the diagnostic that locates such loops; both switches default
off and the added hot-path cost when disabled is one predicted-not-taken
branch per instruction and per data access.

Frozen 48 kHz all-output PCM is bit-identical with the skip off and on while
440,668 iterations were skipped (a65077eb...). The live 44.1 kHz/q32 fast
preset recorded zero PipeWire underruns in both the boot and playback
windows with 444,477 iterations skipped. A matched interleaved ABBA measured
819.6% against 1036.3% average speed, +26.4% with complete separation.

The per-timeslice read-set verification resolves each live-in read to a
direct host pointer at arm time, so steady-state verification is a flat
compare loop with no handler dispatch; any entry that does not resolve to
plain memory keeps the handler-path verification for the whole set.

